    {
      "id": "cls.FullTextSearch",
      "name_local": "FullTextSearch",
      "name_en": "FullTextSearch",
      "kind": "collection",
      "category_keys": [
        "global_context",
        "runtime",
        "full_text_search"
      ],
      "signature": "FullTextSearch",
      "description": "The base's full-text search: finding records by the words of their fields. A global of the server, reached by name.\n\nWHAT IS INDEXED is the metadata's answer: a string attribute whose Full-text search property is on - of a catalog, a document or a chart, of their tabular sections, and the Description and Code of a catalog or a chart. Nothing else keeps a list of them.\n\nTHE INDEX KEEPS ITSELF. A record's words are written with the record, in the same transaction, and dropped when it is deleted: there is no queue and nothing to run after a write. What is left to UpdateIndex is the BUILD - the records written before a field's flag was switched on, before the mode was, or since ClearIndex. IndexTrue says whether anything is left to build.\n\nTHE MODE IS THE BASE'S - one for every session, kept in the base, changed with the Data administration right. A base where nobody switched it on answers FullTextSearchMode.Disable; switching it off empties the index.\n\nWith the mouse: Administration - Full-text search index switches the mode and builds the index; Tools - Find in data searches.",
      "syntax_block": "List = FullTextSearch.CreateList(\"front wheel\", 20);\nList.FirstPart();",
      "parameters": "",
      "return_descr": "",
      "example": "List = FullTextSearch.CreateList(\"front wheel\", 20);\nList.FirstPart();\nfor (i = 0; i < List.Count(); i++) {\n    Message(List.Get(i).Presentation);\n}",
      "availability": "Server",
      "see_also": [
        "cls.FullTextSearch.GetFullTextSearchMode",
        "cls.FullTextSearch.SetFullTextSearchMode",
        "cls.FullTextSearch.IndexTrue",
        "cls.FullTextSearch.UpdateIndex",
        "cls.FullTextSearch.ClearIndex",
        "cls.FullTextSearch.UpdateDate",
        "cls.FullTextSearch.CreateList",
        "cls.FullTextSearchList",
        "enum.FullTextSearchMode"
      ],
      "reviewed": false
    },
    {
      "id": "cls.FullTextSearch.GetFullTextSearchMode",
      "name_local": "GetFullTextSearchMode",
      "name_en": "GetFullTextSearchMode",
      "kind": "method",
      "category_keys": [
        "global_context",
        "runtime",
        "full_text_search"
      ],
      "signature": "FullTextSearch.GetFullTextSearchMode() : FullTextSearchMode",
      "description": "The base's full-text search mode, as it is kept in the base. Nothing saved yet reads as FullTextSearchMode.Disable. A mode this build does not know is refused with its number.",
      "syntax_block": "Mode = FullTextSearch.GetFullTextSearchMode();",
      "parameters": "",
      "return_descr": "FullTextSearchMode.",
      "example": "if (FullTextSearch.GetFullTextSearchMode() = FullTextSearchMode.Disable) {\n    Message(\"Full-text search is off\");\n}",
      "availability": "Server",
      "see_also": [
        "cls.FullTextSearch",
        "cls.FullTextSearch.SetFullTextSearchMode",
        "enum.FullTextSearchMode"
      ],
      "reviewed": false
    },
    {
      "id": "cls.FullTextSearch.SetFullTextSearchMode",
      "name_local": "SetFullTextSearchMode",
      "name_en": "SetFullTextSearchMode",
      "kind": "procedure",
      "category_keys": [
        "global_context",
        "runtime",
        "full_text_search"
      ],
      "signature": "FullTextSearch.SetFullTextSearchMode(mode : FullTextSearchMode)",
      "description": "Switches the base's full-text search on or off, for every session. Needs the Data administration right. Switched on, the index starts empty and every write from then on keeps it - UpdateIndex builds what was written before. Switched off, the index is emptied and no write keeps it. A mode that is not a member of FullTextSearchMode is refused.",
      "syntax_block": "FullTextSearch.SetFullTextSearchMode(FullTextSearchMode.Enable);",
      "parameters": "mode - a member of FullTextSearchMode: Enable or Disable.",
      "return_descr": "",
      "example": "FullTextSearch.SetFullTextSearchMode(FullTextSearchMode.Enable);\nFullTextSearch.UpdateIndex();",
      "availability": "Server",
      "see_also": [
        "cls.FullTextSearch",
        "cls.FullTextSearch.GetFullTextSearchMode",
        "cls.FullTextSearch.UpdateIndex",
        "enum.FullTextSearchMode"
      ],
      "reviewed": false
    },
    {
      "id": "cls.FullTextSearch.IndexTrue",
      "name_local": "IndexTrue",
      "name_en": "IndexTrue",
      "kind": "method",
      "category_keys": [
        "global_context",
        "runtime",
        "full_text_search"
      ],
      "signature": "FullTextSearch.IndexTrue() : boolean",
      "description": "Whether nothing is left to build: every object with indexed fields is built with exactly those fields, and nothing is indexed for an object that has none any more. Writes never make it False - they keep the index themselves; a field's flag switched on or off, the mode switched on and ClearIndex do. False while the mode is off.",
      "syntax_block": "Built = FullTextSearch.IndexTrue();",
      "parameters": "",
      "return_descr": "Boolean.",
      "example": "while (!FullTextSearch.IndexTrue()) {\n    FullTextSearch.UpdateIndex(true);\n}",
      "availability": "Server",
      "see_also": [
        "cls.FullTextSearch",
        "cls.FullTextSearch.UpdateIndex",
        "cls.FullTextSearch.UpdateDate"
      ],
      "reviewed": false
    },
    {
      "id": "cls.FullTextSearch.UpdateIndex",
      "name_local": "UpdateIndex",
      "name_en": "UpdateIndex",
      "kind": "procedure",
      "category_keys": [
        "global_context",
        "runtime",
        "full_text_search"
      ],
      "signature": "FullTextSearch.UpdateIndex(portion : boolean = false)",
      "description": "Builds the index for the records it does not hold yet: those written before a field's flag was switched on, before the mode was, or since ClearIndex. Records are read as they are stored - their modules are not run. Each portion of records is indexed in a transaction of its own, so a stop between portions keeps what was built. Refused while the mode is off. Needs the Data administration right.\n\nONE ARGUMENT. There is no merge argument: every write merges its record into the index. A call written with two arguments - UpdateIndex(merge, portion) - is refused and says so, because its first argument would be read as portion and its second lost. Write UpdateIndex(portion).",
      "syntax_block": "FullTextSearch.UpdateIndex(portion);",
      "parameters": "portion - True to index one portion of records (500) and return; IndexTrue then says whether to call again. Left out - False: everything left is built.",
      "return_descr": "",
      "example": "// a scheduled job: one portion each run, until the index is built\nif (!FullTextSearch.IndexTrue()) {\n    FullTextSearch.UpdateIndex(true);\n}",
      "availability": "Server",
      "see_also": [
        "cls.FullTextSearch",
        "cls.FullTextSearch.IndexTrue",
        "cls.FullTextSearch.ClearIndex"
      ],
      "reviewed": false
    },
    {
      "id": "cls.FullTextSearch.ClearIndex",
      "name_local": "ClearIndex",
      "name_en": "ClearIndex",
      "kind": "procedure",
      "category_keys": [
        "global_context",
        "runtime",
        "full_text_search"
      ],
      "signature": "FullTextSearch.ClearIndex()",
      "description": "Empties the index: nothing is found until UpdateIndex builds it again. The mode is not changed, and writes go on indexing their records. Needs the Data administration right.",
      "syntax_block": "FullTextSearch.ClearIndex();",
      "parameters": "",
      "return_descr": "",
      "example": "FullTextSearch.ClearIndex();\nFullTextSearch.UpdateIndex();",
      "availability": "Server",
      "see_also": [
        "cls.FullTextSearch",
        "cls.FullTextSearch.UpdateIndex"
      ],
      "reviewed": false
    },
